<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Turkish strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  Sentences use the polite "siz"; buttons use the imperative of Turkish iOS ("Kaydet", "Vazgeç").
  A Turkish noun after a number stays singular ("5 atak"), so both plural forms are the same.
  Upper case comes from uppercaseInAppLanguage, which gives "İ" for "i" (plan, section 2.1).
-->
